{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) at 0.591 acc, while image-only resnet50 is very weak (0.208 acc). The critical open question is whether combining the strong RNA signal with the weak image signal via multimodal fusion yields any benefit over the RNA-only baseline. This experiment (config_018: multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) directly extends the best-performing RNA configuration by adding the image modality with the simplest fusion strategy. It tests whether the image carries any complementary information not captured by RNA alone. This is the highest-information next step because: (1) it answers the fundamental multimodal question before investing further in image-encoder or fusion-variant experiments, (2) it builds on the strongest validated RNA setup (pca_n2000 + multiprofile + avgpool), and (3) the result will decisively guide whether to pursue weighted fusion, better image encoders (ViT-L), or refocus entirely on RNA-encoder improvements. Under a limited budget, resolving the 'does multimodal help at all?' question before branching into 30+ multimodal variants is the most efficient use of the next experiment."
}

